# pnpm change verification

When editing `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, overrides, or dependency versions:

1. Run `pnpm install` and confirm it completes.
2. For security work, run `pnpm audit` (or project audit script) before claiming hardened.
3. Do not leave deprecated overrides — prefer bumping to supported versions when asked.

If `engineStrict`, `trustPolicy`, or `minimumReleaseAge` are enabled, treat install failures as blocking — adjust config or document required exceptions.
